      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Let's have a roostertail party or sit in the roosterpit of a plane?\nI've heard other things like \"wanko\" (Japanese for dog) being turned into \"minko\" (could have been worse like keeping the \"a\" instead of the \"i\").\nWord filters are often stupid especially when they only contain English words and they are often over aggressive.\nI assume swear words from other languages are likely not blocked. Because if you'd do that for every language there wouldn't be many words left.\nA common quirk of languages is it to use very common harmless words and use them to describe naughty things. So every language has an endless list of words that describe certain body parts.\nI'm pretty sure the VRC team didn't manually create the list. But maybe they should opt to use a less aggressive one.\nAnd maybe don't do the stupid replace with a similar sounding word thing. That can be confusing because some people might not directly notice that's a word filter problem.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
